,{"class":309},[295,1722,626],{"class":305},[295,1724,1725],{"class":309},"participant",[295,1727,313],{"class":305},[295,1729,1609],{"class":309},[295,1731,363],{"class":402},[295,1733,1734,1736,1738,1741,1743,1746,1748,1751,1753,1755,1757,1760],{"class":297,"line":457},[295,1735,428],{"class":301},[295,1737,1434],{"class":305},[295,1739,1740],{"class":309},"orders",[295,1742,626],{"class":305},[295,1744,1745],{"class":348},"findByOrganization",[295,1747,352],{"class":402},[295,1749,1750],{"class":309},"caller",[295,1752,626],{"class":305},[295,1754,642],{"class":309},[295,1756,313],{"class":305},[295,1758,1759],{"class":309}," status",[295,1761,363],{"class":402},[295,1763,1764],{"class":297,"line":462},[295,1765,454],{"class":305},[295,1767,1768],{"class":297,"line":493},[295,1769,515],{"class":305},[269,1771,1772,1775,1776,1202,1779,1202,1781,1784],{},[273,1773,1774],{},"context.participant"," is the participant the gateway authenticated on the calling connection, serialized with its scope discriminator and ids (",[273,1777,1778],{},"type",[273,1780,642],{},[273,1782,1783],{},"applicationId","). It is absent only for an invocation that originated inside the platform with no participant bound, such as a scheduled job.",[269,1786,1787,1790,1791,1794,1795,1202,1798,1801,1802,1805,1806,1809],{},[273,1788,1789],{},"requireParticipant"," is the counterpart of a Java service's ",[273,1792,1793],{},"securityContext.requireParticipant(OrganizationParticipant.class)",": it returns the participant narrowed by the guard you pass (",[273,1796,1797],{},"isSystemParticipant",[273,1799,1800],{},"isOrganizationParticipant",", or ",[273,1803,1804],{},"isApplicationParticipant","), throws if the invocation carries no participant, and fails the invocation with an ",[273,1807,1808],{},"AuthorizationException"," — the same name a Java refusal carries — when the caller does not hold that scope. The guards alone narrow without throwing, for a method that serves more than one scope.",[2